{"text": "Slide 1\n2026 Year-end Planning - Skoczylas Family\nTidewell & Marchand CPAs - prepared for Bartosz Skoczylas and Noelani Kealoha-Skoczylas\nMeeting Tuesday, November 17, 2026 - Boise office\nClient no. SKO-0412 - confidential\nSpeaker notes: Speaker notes: Dolores presents; Ifeoma Nwachukwu takes notes. Bart joins by phone from the clinic, 208-555-0166. Do not show slide 5 if his mother is in the room.\n\nSlide 2\nAgenda\nWhere 2026 stands vs. 2025\nEstimated tax: Q4 payment and safe harbor\nEntities: Skoczylas Orthodontics, PLLC and NKS Rentals LLC\nKids: 529 plans and Kai's summer wages\nCharitable and family gifts\n\nSlide 3\nWhere 2026 stands\nItem\t2025\t2026 projected\nBart W-2 from the PLLC\t$240,000\t$255,000\nK-1 income, PLLC (EIN 82-3391740)\t$412,880\t$467,000\nNoelani W-2 (school district)\t$68,214\t$70,950\nNKS Rentals, Schedule E (EIN 93-1847265)\t(11,406)\t$6,300\nProjected AGI\t$734k\t$821k\nSpeaker notes: Speaker notes: the rental turned positive because the Garden City duplex at 4108 W. Adams St. was fully let from March 1. Roof replacement $38,400 is capitalized, not expensed.\n\nSlide 4\nEstimated tax\nPaid so far on Form 1040-ES: $52,000 x 3 = $156,000\n110% safe harbor needs $214,720 in total, so Q4 is at least $58,720 by January 15, 2027\nRecommended: pay $75,000 to avoid a spring balance; Form 2210 penalty otherwise about $1,900\nIdaho: $9,500 per quarter; Q3 was paid late (10/02/26)\nSpeaker notes: Speaker notes: Q1-Q3 went on Noelani's American Express ending 98823 through the card processor (fee $962 each time - she wants the points). Recommend IRS Direct Pay or EFTPS from the joint account at Boise Bench Community Bank instead: routing 123394127, account 0071 4482 09. PLLC payroll deposits already use EFTPS, PIN 4471 - Ifeoma holds it, do not put it in the minutes.\n\nSlide 5\nEntities\nPLLC: S-corp since 2019. Reasonable compensation review - Bart's W-2 raised to $255,000\nSection 199A: no QBI deduction above the threshold (specified service trade)\n401(k) profit sharing: fund $46,000 employer contribution by the return due date\nNKS Rentals: Noelani 100% member; second property under contract in Meridian, closing 12/18/2026, price $489,900\n\nSlide 6\nKids\nIDeal 529 contributions: $12,000 joint Idaho deduction, same as 2025\nKai earned $2,140 lifeguarding - Roth IRA at Harrowgate Securities, acct HG-7714-0926, funded $2,000\nGrandmother Stanisława Skoczylas wants to give each child $19,000 - no Form 709 needed at that amount\nChild\tBorn\t529 account\tBalance\nKai Skoczylas\t05/19/2012\tID-529-60441872\t$61,240\nMaile Skoczylas\t2015-08-02\tID-529-60441880\t$44,915\nSpeaker notes: Speaker notes: Maile has type 1 diabetes; pump and supplies ran $7,800 out of pocket, so check the medical floor. Mrs. Skoczylas is in memory care and Bart holds her power of attorney - gifts must come from her own account and be within the POA.\n\nSlide 7\nCharitable\nAppreciated stock to the DAF: 150 shares, basis $4,100, value about $31,500\nCash to Idaho Foodbank Alliance of Ada County: $5,000 pledged, receipt IFA-2026-00871 for the first $2,500\nForm 8283 only if non-cash gifts other than securities exceed the limit\n\nSlide 8\nAction items\nDolores Marchand: Q4 voucher and Idaho estimate to clients by Dec. 4\nBart: sign 401(k) funding letter; send closing statement for Meridian\nNoelani: upload November statements to https://portal.tidewellmarchand.example/c/SKO-0412 (user nkealoha)\nQuestions: dmarchand@tidewellmarchand.example or (208) 555-0119", "kind": "PowerPoint presentation", "detail": "8 slides · 533 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Bartosz Skoczylas", "Noelani Kealoha-Skoczylas", "Dolores", "Ifeoma Nwachukwu", "Bart", "Kai", "Kai Skoczylas", "Stanisława Skoczylas", "Mrs. Skoczylas", "Dolores Marchand", "Noelani"], "companies": ["Skoczylas Family", "Tidewell & Marchand CPAs", "Skoczylas Orthodontics, PLLC", "NKS Rentals LLC", "Boise Bench Community Bank", "Harrowgate Securities", "Idah